note('Author page 3; archive 47. The page passes from finite/unramified-cover categories on the bordered surface to its interior and the punctured sphere, then records the induced fundamental-groupoid map. Its objects are explicitly the rev. étales 1-connexes; dt is retained as an abbreviation. Formula (15) has an uncertain cancelled Σ before Ui, not a live coproduct. The lower paragraph describes a fictitious inclusion obtained by deleting three infinitesimal discs, with “unités” visibly written for their tangent-space models. The slanted margin clarifies a larger three-holed working surface C but writes only “sphère à trous”; the number trois is not supplied in that phrase. No independent proof of the category equivalence has been undertaken. The first arrowhead was examined in crop 048 (440, 160, 1010, 330) and retained; the cancellation after TΣ,Ri remains weak.')
